Same docs: amend the working-set rule from round 3 (proposed). Reserved with the decoded values:
- the error tree (192 bytes per error unit plus 32 per level);
- along the costliest path, 4 KiB of stack per evaluation and the unevaluated-tracking maps (256 + 128 bytes per member, 192 + 96 per item, per evaluation that may copy them);
- once, the largest transient copy (the longest evaluated string, a uniqueItems duplicates map at 192 bytes per item, or a regexp matcher).
Decoded values plus working set must still fit in DecodedLimitFactor times the raw limit (413 otherwise). Measured consequence: arrays of order.json items cost about 59x their raw size and are 413 above about 690 KiB at the 10 MiB default; arrays of 600-value enum items are 413 above about 1.1 MiB. The spec owner's choice among options (a) to (d) from round 3 is still open.
